$$
|\mathcal{F}_i|>\max\left\{\binom{n}{k}-\binom{n-t+1}{k},\binom{kt-1}{k}\right\}
$$

for every $1\leq i\leq t$, then there is a rainbow matching of size $t$. This is a multicolored strengthening of Erdős's matching conjecture, considered independently by Aharoni and Howard. The source presents it as a conjectural statement; its resolution is not established in the supplied text.", "statement_completeness": "full", "post_type": "conjecture", "status": "open", "tags": ["extremal-combinatorics", "hypergraph-theory", "rainbow-matchings"], "importance": "corpus", "source_name": "Hao Huang, Po-Shen Loh and Benny Sudakov, “The size of a hypergraph and its matching number”, arXiv:1107.5544 (2011).", "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1107.5544", "first_stated_year": 2011, "first_stated_year_source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1107.5544", "documented_by_year": null, "documented_by_source_url": null, "references": "Source: https://arxiv.org/abs/1107.5544

